          "summary": "Regional Storefronts — IP Geolocation Routing & AU Storefront Gating",
          "status": {
            "name": "In Refinement",
            "category": "To Do",
            "color": "blue-gray"
          },
          "priority": {
            "name": "High"
          },
          "issuetype": {
            "name": "Story"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "10730",
      "type": {
        "id": "10000",
        "name": "Blocks",
        "inward": "is blocked by",
        "outward": "blocks",
        "self": "https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/issueLinkType/10000"
      },
      "inward_issue": {
        "id": "19335",
        "key": "SFCC-831",
        "self": "https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/issue/19335",
        "fields": {
          "summary": "global/country-language-mismatch — PWA Component",
          "status": {
            "name": "In Progress",
            "category": "In Progress",
            "color": "yellow"
          },
          "priority": {
            "name": "High"
          },
          "issuetype": {
            "name": "Story"
          }
        }
      }
    }
  ],
  "customfield_10231": {
    "value": "1. Given a shopper arrives on a storefront for the first time (see cookie management ACs below) and their IP-detected country does not match the current storefront's shipping region, when the page loads, then the country mismatch slide-out is displayed.\n2. Given the slide-out is displayed, when the shopper views it, then it presents two CTAs: one to redirect them to the correct storefront for their detected location, and one to stay on the current storefront.\n3. Given the slide-out is displayed, when the shopper views it, then it includes a warning that changing their shipping location may remove items from their bag.\n4. Given a shopper clicks the redirect CTA, when they confirm, then they are navigated to the storefront that corresponds to their IP-detected country.\n5. Given a shopper clicks CTA to stay on the current storefront, then the slide-out drawer closes, and the shopper is not redirected.\n6. Given a shopper's IP-detected country matches the current storefront's shipping region, when the page loads, then the slide-out is not displayed.\n7. Given a shopper is on the AU storefront, when they browse the site, then the slide-out is never displayed — AU gating is handled at IP routing level ([SFCC-817]).\n\n*Cookie management for country mismatch:*\n\n# *Given* a shopper dismisses or acts on the country mismatch slide-out\n*When* the interaction is complete\n*Then* a required functional cookie is set in the shopper's browser suppressing the slide-out for X days\n# *Given* the cookie has been set\n*When* the shopper returns to the site within X days\n*Then* the country mismatch slide-out is not shown, regardless of IP/country mismatch\n# *Given* the cookie has expired (after X days)\n*When* the shopper returns to the site and their IP-detected country still does not match the storefront's shipping region\n*Then* the country mismatch slide-out is shown again\n# *Given* the shopper clears their browser cookies\n*When* they return to the site and their IP-detected country does not match the storefront's shipping region\n*Then* the country mismatch slide-out is shown again, as no suppression cookie is present\n\nWe can start with 7 days but needs to be able to be changed."
  }
}

